  "correction_notes": [
    {
      "published_at": "2026-11-04",
      "note": "gemini-3.1-pro-preview produced no run records for this print: every attempt failed with Google's API error \"Your prepayment credits are depleted\", a billing failure on the publisher's own prepaid account, not a quality-gate failure. Its last measured cost (basket cost $0.038953 on 2026-10-25) was carried forward for three days, 2026-10-26 to 2026-10-28, the methodology's limit, and from 2026-10-29 it is excluded. This print is therefore the equal-weighted average of 9 constituents instead of 10. Gemini was the most expensive constituent, so the prints of 2026-10-29 to 2026-11-04 read 29% to 30% below the last print that measured it (2026-10-25, $0.01080). The other nine constituents averaged $0.007669 on 2026-10-25, and these prints range from $0.007569 to $0.007665, so the step comes from the missing constituent, not from a market move. The published figure is correctly computed from the constituents that ran, but it is not comparable with prints that include Gemini."
    }
  ]
